<div class="notice notice-warning">
  <strong>Reservation policy note:</strong>
  The legacy lounge and BBQ reservation policy PDF is still linked for reference, but residents have reported that substantial portions are outdated. Use the current reservation page and contact <a href="mailto:eha-reservations@mit.edu">eha-reservations@mit.edu</a> when in doubt.
</div>
  <h2>Reserving areas of Edgerton</h2>
<ul>
<li>Review the <a href="/assets/uploads/2015/12/reservation_policy.pdf">Policy for Location Use and Reservations</a></li>
<li>Make your reservation <a href="/resources/reservations/">online</a></li>
<li>Print out some <a href="/assets/uploads/2013/09/reservation_sign.pdf">reservation signs</a></li>
<li>To create a guest list for your event, inquire at the front desk or print yourself a <a href="/assets/uploads/2013/09/guest_list.pdf">Temporary Guest List</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Suggest a purchase</h2>
<p>If you would like to suggest that the Edgerton House Association buy something for residents, please email the <a href="mailto:eha-resources@mit.edu">resources chair</a> with your suggestion.</p>
<h2>Transferring within Edgerton</h2>
<p>If you have a renewable housing contract in Edgerton House, you can enter the transfer housing lottery to request a transfer to a different room in Edgerton House. You can read about this process in the <a href="/assets/uploads/2013/09/transfer_lottery_rules2009.pdf">Transfer Lottery Rules</a>. Also check out the <a href="/assets/uploads/2013/09/transfer_cheat_sheet2009.pdf">Transfer Cheat Sheet</a>.</p>
<h2>Leaving Edgerton</h2>
<p>If you are leaving Edgerton as a resident, review the <a href="/assets/uploads/2016/05/REVISED-EDGERTON-HOUSE-TERMINATION-CHECKLIST.pdf">Termination Checklist</a> to make sure you do not forget anything.</p></section>
